<para>What patterns do you notice? Can you use those ideas to find the vertices for the next equation? What do you know about whether it will open up or down?</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="6d96edd7-0ebf-49e9-863f-39010f16baa6" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q5a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e97a365f-1e27-4b93-bd6d-96a10e2e7517" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="4">
    <problem>
      <para>Without graphing, find the coordinates of the vertex of \(y=-(x−4)^2+8\) and determine if it opens up or down.</para>
      <para> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex?</para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is 4.</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q5b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="cc967510-ac1e-4d56-9e53-cfdeb3d963a6" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="8">
