<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="1afdb331-0db4-46fe-935e-44c053021779" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q8a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="06c86bbb-e9b6-4927-8751-95ce8e76aef4" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="-m">
    <problem>
      <para>Use the completed rows of the table to hypothesize about the coordinates of the vertex of the equation in the last row, and whether the parabola opens up or down.</para>
      <para> For the equation \(y=a(x+m)^2+n\), what is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is –\(m\).</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q8b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="8e9f2598-2017-457c-bd50-9015f7ebfbb7" data-problem-comparator="text" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="n">
    <problem>
      <para> For the equation \(y=a(x+m)^2+n\), what is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex of this equation is \(n\).</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Q6c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="10468be6-f473-420b-b5a3-b14329156584" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> For the equation \(y=a(x+m)^2+n\), can you determine if the graph opens up or down with the information you are given? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No, because the direction of opening depends on whether \(a\) is positive or negative.</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
